WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.293 --> 00:00:03.016
I was horrified by what Nemo had done.

2
00:00:03.017 --> 00:00:08.983
No matter what he had suffered at the hands of those men, he had no right to kill them by sinking their ship.

3
00:00:08.984 --> 00:00:14.888
And he had made me a witness to his terrible vengeance, perhaps even an accomplice!

4
00:00:14.889 --> 00:00:19.285
I spent a few hours with Ned and Conseil, who had remained in my cabin.

5
00:00:19.286 --> 00:00:24.118
We did not have much to say, being too stunned by the events of that day.

6
00:00:24.119 --> 00:00:27.017
Later I went to the deserted gallery.

7
00:00:27.018 --> 00:00:32.785
I consulted the instruments, and found that the Nautilus was swiftly heading toward the northern seas.

8
00:00:32.786 --> 00:00:36.935
That night we crossed two hundred leagues of the Atlantic.

9
00:00:36.936 --> 00:00:44.094
I returned to my cabin, but could not sleep because that horrible scene of destruction kept replaying before my eyes.

10
00:00:44.095 --> 00:00:50.578
From that day forward, I lost all track of time because the clocks were stopped onboard.

11
00:00:50.579 --> 00:00:55.261
For the next few weeks, The Nautilus was underwater almost constantly.

12
00:00:55.262 --> 00:00:59.745
There were no new marks on the map, so I had no idea where we were.

13
00:00:59.746 --> 00:01:05.253
I saw nothing of Nemo. As a matter of fact, I didn't see a single crew member.

14
00:01:05.254 --> 00:01:09.499
One morning I awoke suddenly to find Ned standing over me.

15
00:01:09.500 --> 00:01:17.316
"We're going to flee tonight, Professor," he whispered. "There doesn't seem to be anyone in charge anymore. You'll be ready?"

16
00:01:17.317 --> 00:01:21.307
I sat up. "Yes, of course, but where are we?"

17
00:01:21.308 --> 00:01:27.813
"The fog just lifted for a moment and I sighted land about twenty miles away. I don't know what country it is."

18
00:01:27.814 --> 00:01:29.321
"How's the weather?"

19
00:01:29.322 --> 00:01:37.218
"The sea is bad and the wind is violent," replied Ned. "But twenty miles in the small boat doesn't frighten me."

20
00:01:37.219 --> 00:01:40.964
"I'll follow you, Ned, even if the sea swallows us up."

21
00:01:40.965 --> 00:01:46.797
"There," I thought. I had made up my mind and finally agreed to his escape plan. I

22
00:01:46.798 --> 00:01:49.535
dressed quickly and went up to the platform. The

23
00:01:49.536 --> 00:01:56.305
sea was so rough that I could barely keep my balance, but I knew that land was somewhere out there in the fog. I

24
00:01:56.306 --> 00:02:03.202
returned to the empty gallery, both wishing and not wishing to see Nemo. What could I have said to him? Could

25
00:02:03.203 --> 00:02:08.678
I have hid my horror at what he had done? No, it was better that we did not meet. I

26
00:02:08.679 --> 00:02:14.694
stayed by myself all day and avoided Ned and Conseil for fear of betraying our secret. I

27
00:02:14.695 --> 00:02:18.519
dined at six that night, even though I wasn't hungry. I

28
00:02:18.520 --> 00:02:25.956
forced myself to eat so that I might keep up my strength. At half past six, Ned came to my cabin. "We

29
00:02:25.957 --> 00:02:30.186
won't see each other again before our departure at ten o'clock," he said. "The

30
00:02:30.187 --> 00:02:34.837
moon will not have risen yet, so we'll take advantage of the darkness to escape. Come

31
00:02:34.838 --> 00:02:39.012
to the small boat; Conseil and I will be waiting for you there." Ned

32
00:02:39.013 --> 00:02:45.496
left without giving me time to respond. Wishing to check the course of the Nautilus , I went to the gallery.

33
00:02:45.497 --> 00:02:48.575
We were heading northeast at a rapid speed.

34
00:02:48.576 --> 00:02:56.567
I spent the next hour slowly walking around the room and admiring all the natural and man-made treasures that Captain Nemo had collected.

35
00:02:56.568 --> 00:03:02.138
Returning to my room, I dressed warmly and gathered my notes on underwater life.

36
00:03:02.139 --> 00:03:06.242
I stretched out on my bed in an attempt to quiet my nerves.

37
00:03:06.243 --> 00:03:09.470
In my mind I reviewed our months of captivity:

38
00:03:09.471 --> 00:03:21.464
our arrival onboard the submarine, the attack of the natives, the visit to the coral cemetery, the underwater passage to the Mediterranean, the discovery of the South Pole, and everything else that had happened.

39
00:03:21.465 --> 00:03:25.726
All these scenes passed before my eyes as if I were viewing a play.

40
00:03:25.727 --> 00:03:31.702
Captain Nemo seemed to grow enormously, and his features assumed superhuman proportions.

41
00:03:31.703 --> 00:03:37.036
He was no longer my equal but a man of the waters, the genie of the sea.

42
00:03:37.037 --> 00:03:42.528
It was now 9:30. I held my head between my hands to keep it from bursting.

43
00:03:42.529 --> 00:03:48.861
There was another long half hour to wait. After a while I heard the distant sound of organ music.

44
00:03:48.862 --> 00:03:56.028
Captain Nemo was in the gallery, and I had to pass through that room to escape! But it was now nearly ten o'clock.

45
00:03:56.029 --> 00:04:00.441
The moment had come for me to leave my cabin and join my companions.

46
00:04:00.442 --> 00:04:06.353
I crept along the passage until I reached the door of the gallery. I opened the door gently.

47
00:04:06.354 --> 00:04:11.171
The room was completely dark, but the captain was still playing the organ.

48
00:04:11.172 --> 00:04:18.925
I moved so slowly across the room that it took me five full minutes to reach the door to the library.

49
00:04:18.926 --> 00:04:25.584
I was about to open it when a sigh from Captain Nemo nailed me to the spot. I knew that he was standing up.

50
00:04:25.585 --> 00:04:30.830
He came toward me silently, gliding like a ghost rather than walking.

51
00:04:30.831 --> 00:04:36.513
He was sobbing, and I heard him say, "Enough! Enough!"

52
00:04:36.514 --> 00:04:44.155
Was that a confession or at least some expression of remorse? Could he see me there in the darkness? I didn't know.

53
00:04:44.156 --> 00:04:48.814
In desperation I rushed through the library and up the stairs to the platform.

54
00:04:48.815 --> 00:04:52.901
I climbed into the small boat, where I found Ned and Conseil waiting for me.

55
00:04:52.902 --> 00:04:55.322
"Let's go!" I exclaimed.

56
00:04:55.323 --> 00:04:59.139
Ned began to loosen the bolts that held the boat to the submarine.

57
00:04:59.140 --> 00:05:04.480
Suddenly we heard loud voices from below. Had someone discovered our flight?

58
00:05:04.481 --> 00:05:08.458
"Whirlpool! Whirlpool!" voices cried.

59
00:05:08.459 --> 00:05:12.115
"They're shouting about a giant whirlpool!" said Conseil. "They're

60
00:05:12.116 --> 00:05:14.282
not after us." My

61
00:05:14.283 --> 00:05:23.457
heart sunk. Apparently we were now in those Norwegian waters famous for a dangerous whirlpool. No vessel had ever survived it. We

62
00:05:23.458 --> 00:05:34.362
would never know if this had happened accidentally or if Captain Nemo had deliberately sent the Nautilus straight into the whirlpool in order to destroy the submarine and everyone aboard! Dreadful

63
00:05:34.363 --> 00:05:40.616
sounds filled our ears as the submarine spiraled toward the center of the whirlpool. Dizzy,

64
00:05:40.617 --> 00:05:44.933
and overcome with fear, I grabbed Conseil's hand. "Hold

65
00:05:44.934 --> 00:05:50.441
on!" shouted Ned. "We may be saved if we cling to the Nautilus and—" Just

66
00:05:50.442 --> 00:05:55.695
then we heard a crashing sound and the small boat was torn from the submarine. My

67
00:05:55.696 --> 00:05:59.322
head struck something metal, and I lost consciousness. I

68
00:05:59.323 --> 00:06:05.584
woke up in a Norwegian fisherman's cottage. How I got here, I have no idea. To

69
00:06:05.585 --> 00:06:12.155
my great relief, my two companions were safe and sound too, and at my bedside holding my hands. I

70
00:06:12.156 --> 00:06:16.354
must now wait for a month for the next steamship to France. So

71
00:06:16.355 --> 00:06:20.989
it is here where I'm reviewing my amazing adventures with Captain Nemo. I

72
00:06:20.990 --> 00:06:28.751
traveled 20,000 leagues under the sea with him, but I have no idea what happened to him or his beloved Nautilus .

73
00:06:28.752 --> 00:06:34.068
I still have so many questions: Will the waves ever carry his manuscript to land?

74
00:06:34.069 --> 00:06:40.243
Will I learn his real name? Will the nationality of the sunken ship reveal his home country?

75
00:06:40.244 --> 00:06:46.481
Will I ever know what happened to his family and why he needed to seek revenge so desperately?

76
00:06:46.482 --> 00:06:55.124
I hope these answers come. But I also hope that Captain Nemo's powerful vessel conquered the whirlpool and that he still inhabits the sea.

77
00:06:55.125 --> 00:07:04.984
Perhaps contemplating the wonders of the sea will restore his soul—and forever extinguish the spirit of vengeance that burns within him.

